@bupt-lxc Thank you for the thorough hardware validation and the follow-up — much appreciated. I have incorporated a442cfeae1 into this PR (branch head now 2dfc7d1c55, your authorship preserved):

- encoder SWA now reuses the compressed MTP mask in banded sparse mode (`mask = self.mtp_mask if is_swa_layer else None`), fixing the 561002 rejection;
- the non-hybrid FIA call receives the same explicit window bounds (encoder SWA `W`/`W`, decoder SWA `W`/`0`).

Your 5-model replay plus the deterministic boundary test made this an easy call. The PR is still gated on the `run-ci` label for the downstream checks — maintainers, a `run-ci` label when convenient would let CI exercise the updated head.

